---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteMeta } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={`About ${siteMeta.name}.`}>
  <article class="page">
    <p class="identity">{siteMeta.name} · about</p>
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      Replace this with a compact biography: where you are based, what you work on, and the thread
      that connects your interests. The tone here is intentionally plain and direct, closer to a
      well-kept note than a pitch deck.
    </p>

    <h2>Work</h2>
    <p>
      A good personal site makes your work legible without making visitors fight the layout. This
      section can hold your current role, research agenda, selected projects, or collaborations.
    </p>

    <h2>Interests</h2>
    <p>
      Systems, tools for thought, machine learning infrastructure, writing, photography, maps,
      public transport, and whatever else makes the page feel unmistakably yours.
    </p>

    <h2>Colophon</h2>
    <p>
      This site is built with Astro, Markdown, and a little CSS. It is static by default, deploys
      cleanly to GitHub Pages, and should be easy to carry somewhere else later.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
